99 of americans have at least one  television in their home  could you survive without a television  hey everyone  welcome to yessi tv where you can find  weekly videos on minimalism  and healthy living to help you live a  simpler happier life  this week's video is a bit similar to  last week's video on why i do not have  social media  and we're going to be talking about why  i do not own a television  so i'm going to share with you my six  reasons for why we tossed ours in the  first place  and if you stick to the end i will share  with you my three tips for how you can  ditch yours for good  reason number one conversation killer  for most people their days are spent  very busy shuffling between work  school sports daily to-do's take out the  trash  we didn't want our precious family time  to be spent sitting in front of a screen  each person in their own world not  really talking to one another  when we first decided to get rid of our  tv i remember being worried  about how we were gonna host friends and  family members  and whether or not they were gonna be  bored or we were gonna have things to do  or to talk about  then i remembered a time when i visited  a friend and we spent three hours just  talking and to her husband's surprised  face when he asked  you didn't go anywhere you didn't do  anything  but talk we laughed that day as we told  him  yeah we talked  being able to enjoy each other's company  and talk about our lives  goals and ideas became a priority for my  husband and i  and having a television only became a  barrier  reason number two negativity  the average child will watch 8 000  murders before completing elementary  school  and by the age of 18 the average adult  will have watched  200 000 acts of violence  tell me what your thoughts are i want to  know do you think that constantly seeing  acts of violence and crime  can change your perspective of the world  at least for me personally i know that  watching things like the news  only brings up feelings of me of anger  worry  and anxiety as i see all of the things  that are going wrong in the world  after all television is made to make  money and happy stories with happy  endings and no action  does not make money so i ditched the big  screen of negativity  the third reason why we decided to ditch  the tv is because it did not in line  with our values  not to make this long i will only give  you one example but we  highly value respect for our elders and  for our parents  when i was a child if i even so much as  raised my voice at my parents  i was whooped no i'm not talking about  whether or not you should whoop your  children  but what i mean is at a young age it was  very much ingrained in me from my  parents that i was to respect my elders  and to respect my parents  and i know from watching children's  shows things like disney channel  often show children that the dad is the  dumb person  and that they can talk back to their  parents and this is a funny thing and  it's a cool thing and that is not  something that we want to teach our  children  and most cartoons today are not as clean  humored and family oriented as they were  at least when i was a child at least for  us  most of what is on tv does not reflect  the kinds of characteristics that we  want in our children  and the value of respect is only one  example  reason number four we fall prey to  advertising  by the age of 65 the average american  will have seen  two million commercials did you ever sit  through a commercial and all of a sudden  realize that you need that dyson vacuum  cleaner  or suddenly feel hungry after seeing a  commercial of a juicy cheeseburger  we are constantly being told that we  need more that we need that new necklace  that we need that new weight loss plan  that avocado slicer or that hot dog  slicer  ooh hot dog slicer that's kind of cute  how much is that  reason number five is health research  has shown  time and time again that a positive  mindset can actually improve your  overall health and your lifespan as well  and this makes sense because as i've  mentioned in previous videos  stress triggers inflammation which  triggers disease  so on one side not having a television  can help me be healthier as a person  because by removing the negative  influences from television  i am increasing my positive mindset and  therefore  being able to be happier as a person and  healthier  but on the other side i can also be  healthier  physically as well americans are  becoming increasingly more sedentary in  their lifestyle  a research study reported on ergonomic  trends reported that people who sit for  six hours or more and have a sedentary  lifestyle  have a 71 higher mortality rate  71 those stats were scary to me but the  truth is that we could all use a little  bit more movement and if we're sitting  in front of a screen  we're not getting movement now when i  get bored i actually get up and do  something  okay sometimes it's sitting and reading  a book but most of the time i get up i  play with my daughter i go for a walk  or i start a project or a craft that i  forgotten about or that i had  procrastinated  and lastly reason number six  productivity and procrastination  there's only 24 hours in a day so of  course the more time you spend doing one  activity  the less time you have doing another  according to this bar graph from the  american bureau of labor statistics  most americans spend at least two hours  a day watching television  this fluctuates based on age employment  status and other factors  but you get the picture if you have two  hours to spend on watching television  that's two hours that you could have  spent doing other things  maybe you have a project that you've  been putting off maybe you could use a  little more sleep  more time with your family or more time  to work on skills to improve yourself  and your career not having a television  can free  so much of your time so that you can  spend it to making your life better  now that i've shared with you my six  reasons for why we just the tv  i can share with you my three tips for  how you can say bye bye to the black  screen  but first did you know the average  american has at least two televisions in  their home  how many do you have let me know in the  comments  my tip number one is if you are not  quite ready to part ways with your tv  and it's still a huge part of your life  ease into it  adopt a household rule when tv and  electronics are not allowed at specific  times  for us for example this is bedtime for  kiddos  and meal times if someone calls us or  messages us  during bedtime for the kiddos or while  we're eating dinner we will not answer  the phone until  after we're finished and for my husband  and i it actually became  very important that we never answer the  phone during meal times  even if the kids are not around because  it's important to us that we keep  dating even after being married because  life gets busy and you go your separate  ways  and you lose sight of one another and  for us it was a huge priority to let our  kids know that we value them enough to  dedicate time specifically to them  tip number two if you've moved past the  reluctant stage and you're ready to toss  it  but you worry that you might regret it  unplug it and put it in an area that's  hard for you to reach  for me i did this for actually about two  weeks before we actually said let's just  do it  we unplugged it and we moved it into the  attic not only did this make it harder  for us to actually go get it plug it in  if we wanted to watch something  but for us to have it for two weeks put  away we could realize  oh you know what this isn't so bad we  are living a pretty normal life without  it and we can deal without it  and tip number three if you've already  done number two now fill the void with  something that brings you  joy on our tv stand we placed an oil  painting that my husband made of the  sunset on our first date  when i missed the tv the first few days  this made me happy and it made me  remember  why we did it in the first place you can  use family photos  board games artwork whatever brings you  joy and whatever reminds you what's most  valuable to you  and what's most important to you in your  life and for sticking to the end my  bonus tip for you is don't see this as a  loss but as a gain  you're not losing a television you're  gaining quality time with the ones you  love  meaningful relationships and the  opportunity to work on improving  yourself as a person  guys our time is ticking and we'll run  out someday  what do you want to do and accomplish in  your life and who and what matters most  to you  your time is precious so use it wisely  that's it for today guys if you like  this video please give it a thumbs up  and subscribe so that you won't miss out  on my weekly videos  i thank you so much for watching and i  hope to see you in the next one
 

